WEBVTT

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.320
What's wrong, Rio?

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.780
Do you sense something again?

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.260
I-I'm okay. It's nothing...

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.390
<i>It's that dream again... What exactly is it...?</i>

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:41.320
These are the last ruins...

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:45.050
It's the location where the 
sixth and seventh Number are being held.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:51.070
And it's also the place where the legends of the two Barian Emperors we haven't met are.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:53.930
Barians we haven't met yet...

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.440
Yuma... What happened to Kaito?

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.980
Ah... He said he had to check into some things.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.830
Probably about Misael...

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.390
Then we'll use these members for this adventure.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:07.300
Yeah.

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:11.660
As you can see, the distance between the two Numbers is pretty close.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.890
Could they be in the same place?

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.840
Anyway, we just gotta obtain the last two 
Numbers one way or another!

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:22.880
So let's go!

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.760
The "Bringin' It Yuma Airline" is taking off!

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.620
So the Number spirit named Jinlong

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.170
was related to you when you were a human?

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.430
That's right. But I have no intention of believing it.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:44.470
I am a proud warrior of Barian.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:47.040
There's no way I'm related to those inferior humans!

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.800
I'm not going to believe it either.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.070
But I am interested in the remaining ruins.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:57.390
The legends for Nasch and Merag should be there.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.830
That means you actually do believe them, right?

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.070
It does not!

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.150
I just want some clues regarding those two.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.500
The powers of the Seven Barian Emperors will change if they're there.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.940
We must find the remaining Numbers no matter what.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:16.980
Say, Astral...

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:22.660
Those Barian guys... are really human, right?

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:26.300
I don't doubt the memories I got from the Numbers.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.320
Do the Barians exist similarly to the way you do?

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:36.080
If the Astral World is the same 
as the Barian World, it's likely the case.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.370
Why did those guys become Barians?

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:44.930
There could be something the legends share in common that allowed the Barians to reincarnate.

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:47.970
It's not a good idea to get too deeply involved with them.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.120
Shark!

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.230
If you don't throw away your sentimental feelings, you'll only slow us down again.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:02.030
Hey, Shark... Why are you fighting the Barians?

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:05.640
That should be obvious. They used Rio and me!

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.890
This is their atonement for that!

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:12.240
But didn't you already forgive Tron and Faker.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.220
It's not that I forgave them.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.910
My will to fight them disappeared.
 That's the only reason I stopped.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:22.920
I guess it's a philosophy of yours 
to not bring emotions into your Duels.

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:26.400
It's fine if your reason to fight is always for yourself.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.720
That's why I'm a lone wolf.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:32.480
Shark...

00:03:56.110 --> 00:04:03.660
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.710
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:14.170
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:17.720
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:22.600
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:28.940
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:32.150
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:35.030
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:39.660
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.740
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:51.210
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:14.000
Hey! Are the ruins really located here?!

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:15.670
"Invitation to the Bottom of the Ocean!
 Shark's Dreamlike Memory."

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:17.630
The coordinates point here! It has to be!

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.760
<i>Come to me.</i>

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.800
Hey, Rio! Rio! What's wrong?

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:29.180
I-It's nothing...

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:35.640
Anyway, it seems we should take
 refuge in this area for the time being.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.270
All right!

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.230
W-Wait!

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.270
The ship's power seems to be stopping!

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:53.410
So that means the ship won't move beyond this point...

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:58.710
<i>Come to me... Come to me...</i>

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:02.000
Who?! Who are you?!

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:05.170
Who's calling me?!

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.340
R-Rio?

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:11.010
Wh-What the?

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.390
Wh-What's wrong?

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:17.730
<i>Come to me... Now come to me...</i>

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:20.810
The lights went out.

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:22.940
What was that just now?

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.990
Rio...! Rio! Rio!

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:31.410
The monitor!

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:36.250
Rio?

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.460
Wh-What's she doing out there?

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:48.550
Sh-Shark!

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.640
<i>Come to me...</i>

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.640
<i>Come on down...</i>

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:00.560
Rio!!

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:06.900
Rio!!

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.070
Shark!

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.120
Shark!

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.670
I'm gonna bring it!

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:27.590
Yuma!

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.550
<i>Shark...! Rio...!</i>

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:37.470
Yuma...! Yuma!!

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.940
Yuma!!

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:53.200
Yuma... Yuma!

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:54.780
Wake up, Yuma!

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.040
H-Huh? Shark? Astral?

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.040
Wh-Where are we?

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:03.370
I'm not sure.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:07.460
I lost consciousness when I was swallowed by the water.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:12.880
But this would appear to be another land below the ocean.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:15.430
Whoa! The ocean's in the sky!

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:17.430
And Rio also...

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:20.020
...came to this place.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:29.440
That's...

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.070
What the?

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:45.920
What is that...?

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:51.010
Is this...some kind of labyrinth?

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:55.300
Yeah.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:08:59.760
What's wrong?

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.430
These are my dad's coins.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.190
The Numbers must be here.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:15.110
Rio has a mysterious power...

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.740
Rio's been sensing something long before we came here.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.410
That power may have lead her down here.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:29.130
That power...? The Numbers...?

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:31.420
<i>Come to me...</i>

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:45.140
This is... Rio's card...

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.690
Hey, Yuma-

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:49.400
What?!

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.660
But really, how long does this maze go on for?

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:01.660
It would seem that blindly advancing won't get us out of here.

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:04.370
We aren't blindly advancing!

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.960
The thing about mazes is that, no matter where you go,

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.830
there's only one wall blocking the outside.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:12.840
If you keep going straight from the entrance along the wall, you'll eventually get out.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.260
I see.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.720
Not a bad plan for you.

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:19.590
How 'bout it? Wanna try it, Shark?

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.760
H-He's gone!

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.100
Hey, Shark!

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.600
Where are you, Shark?!

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:27.770
Hey!

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:33.860
This is weird. We didn't go that far since we entered the maze.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.730
There's no entrance to get out of!

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:40.030
It would appear that common sense holds no bounds here.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:44.580
Because we've been in the same place this entire time.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:45.040
You're kidding!

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:46.660
It's true.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.790
Once I see something, I do not forget it.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.880
We've passed this broken wall three times already.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:56.300
So we've lost the entrance?

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:57.720
So it would seem.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:58.880
No way...

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:03.300
Now I'm done playing Mr. Nice guy!

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:06.020
Don't look down on the son of an adventurer!

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.150
Yuma! Look up ahead!

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:15.360
Huh?!

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:18.280
A-A wall's being created!

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:21.450
O-Over here too?

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:25.780
What's up with this?! Now we can't get outta here!

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:31.290
It would seem this labyrinth intends 
to hinder our path by all means.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.000
Then Shark also...

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:39.920
<i>Come to me.</i>

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:40.670
Who are you?!

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.510
Are you luring me in?

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:49.520
<i>Come to me... Come to me!</i>

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:54.440
That's...

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:09.660
R-Rio!

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.000
Rio, that's a Number!

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.210
Rio...?

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:23.970
I have been waiting for you, Ryouga Kamishiro.

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:27.430
Who the hell are you?

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:31.350
My name is Abyss!

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:37.060
The spirit of a Number...

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.530
Did you control Rio in order to call me out here?!

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:42.950
It is your fate to fight against me.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:46.910
It is time to awaken, thou holding my power!

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:51.620
I have no idea what you're planning, but I'll be your opponent!

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:52.540
Now let Rio go!

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:54.330
Of course.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:57.750
If you are able to defeat me in a Duel, that is.

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:02.170
Fine then! I'll crush you flat and get Rio back!

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.260
Duel Disk, set!

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.550
D-Gazer, set!

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:15.440
Duel!!

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:19.520
Yuma!

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:23.650
Shark! Rio-<i>san</i>!

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:27.320
I hope they're all okay...

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:28.030
Huh...?

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:33.580
What?

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.500
Huh? Y-You're...!

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:42.170
The fact that you guys are here
 means that the Numbers are also here.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.720
I-I don't know anything about no Numbers!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:47.970
The guys just jumped into the ocean and went missing, is all!

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:49.300
The ocean?

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:51.930
I see.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.060
Just what could be down under the ocean...?

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.400
Here goes! My turn! Draw!

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.320
I Summon Big Jaws!

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:15.750
And when I Summon a Fish-Type Monster on my field,

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:18.420
I can Special Summon this guy from my hand!

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:20.920
Show yourself, Shark Sucker!

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:26.630
I Overlay the Level Three Big Jaws and Shark Sucker!

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:31.430
I use these two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.010
Xyz Summon!

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:36.180
A crimson spear emerges from the pitch black darkness!

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:38.890
Come forth, Black Ray Lancer!

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:41.860
I can't attack on the first turn.

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:46.110
So I set one card. Turn end!

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.410
My turn! Draw!

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:52.490
I Summon Gorgonic Golem!

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:03.040
And when I Summon a Gorgonic Monster on my field,

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:07.130
I can Special Summon Gorgonic Gargoyle from my hand!

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:13.260
Behold, Ryouga! My power!

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:18.140
I Overlay the Level Three Gorgonic Golem and Gargoyle!

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:23.400
I use the two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.020
Xyz Summon!

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:28.690
Show yourself, Gorgonic Guardian!

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:37.660
1600 Attack Points...

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:41.290
But Black Ray Lancer's Attack Power is 2100.

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:43.460
You won't be able to stand against it.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:46.170
Hmph, are you certain?

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:50.220
I activate Gorgonic Guardian's effect!

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:52.760
I detach one Overlay Unit,

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:55.850
negate the effects of one Monster on the field,

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:58.930
and reduce its Attack Points to zero!

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:03.770
B-Black Ray Lancer was...!

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:05.730
Not done yet!

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:12.610
When Gorgonic Guardian is on the field, all Monsters with zero Attack Points are destroyed!

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:14.320
Say what?!

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.380
Gorgonic Guardian! Direct Attack!

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:37.100
I set one card face-down. Turn end.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:44.520
You plan to take Rio back looking so pathetic, Ryouga?

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:52.490
What is this light...?

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.780
Th-This is...!

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:02.830
Ah... What?!

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:06.580
Wh-What is this place...?

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:14.420
Impossible...! Why am I dressed like this...?!

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.970
Just what is going on here...?

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:21.930
Dear brother.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:32.280
It is nearly time. Everyone is waiting for you.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.780
R-Rio...!

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:49.170
- Our king!
 - Your majesty!

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:53.420
They're all praising their great king.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.920
Me? A king?

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:58.800
<i>What is this...?</i>

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:02.470
<i>Could this be the memories of this country...?</i>

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:04.180
Your majesty! Your majesty!

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:06.140
Your majesty, there's an enemy attack!

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:07.850
Enemy?!

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.880
That's...the enemy?!

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:44.100
Fire back!

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:17.460
Vector!

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:23.680
That's the King of Madness who has invaded, slaughtered and plundered countless!

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:26.640
Why is Vector...?

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:40.900
<i>Did this guy just show me a vision...?</i>

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.780
<i>What in the world is he planning?!</i>

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.370
My turn! Draw!

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:50.500
<i>if I play Attack Mode, Gorgonic Guardian's effect</i>

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.540
<i>will only destroy my Monster again.</i>

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:55.750
I set a Monster in Face-Down Defense Position!

00:19:58.000 --> 00:19:59.760
I'll end my turn there.

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.720
<i>Gorgonic Guardian has 1600 Attack Points.</i>

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:08.010
<i>The card I set is the 1600 Defense Power Skull Kraken.</i>

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:12.850
<i>With this, I shouldn't take any damage next turn...</i>

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:15.690
My turn! Draw!

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:20.190
Is that supposed to protect you from Gorgonic Guardian's attack?

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:23.530
I activate a Magic Card on the field!

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:25.370
Gorgon Charming!

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:30.580
This card switches a face-down Monster on the field into face-up Defense Position.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:32.000
What?!

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.960
Oh no! Skull Kraken was...!

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:42.880
I activate Gorgonic Guardian's effect!

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:45.430
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:50.810
I negate the effect of a Monster on the field and reduce its Attack Power to zero!

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:57.110
And I activate Gorgonic Guardian's other effect!

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:01.360
It destroys all Monsters on the field with zero Attack Points!

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:09.080
Then I activate the Equip Magic, Xyz Unit, from my hand!

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:12.910
This card becomes an Equip Card on an Xyz Monster,

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:18.130
and the equipped Monster's Attack Points rise by 200 points times its rank!

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:21.130
Gorgonic Guardian, Direct Attack!

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:29.720
Shit! What're we going to do?!

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:32.680
Huh?

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:35.770
Wh-What the?!

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:43.190
Durbe!

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:45.700
Yuma. Astral.

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:47.700
What are you doing here?!

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:50.740
I followed you guys.

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:53.540
We cannot afford to let any more Numbers go.

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:56.080
You want to settle things right now?!

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:59.330
You are an opponent that must be defeated sooner or later.

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:01.500
It's not a bad deal, really.

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:05.050
Durbe...

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:23.730
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:26.280
